title: Remove deprecated treasury spend_local and remove_approval
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Removed `spend_local` and `remove_approval` (deprecated by May 2025), plus the related public
    getters, and dropped the legacy drain loop from `spend_funds` along with its
    `on_initialize_proposals` benchmark and weight entries.

    The legacy `ProposalCount` / `Proposals` / `Approvals` storage now lives behind `migration::v0`
    aliases. `migration::MigrateV0ToV1` pays approved proposals out of the pot, refunds every
    proposer's bond and then deletes that storage, and bumps the pallet storage version from 0 to
    1 so the step runs once. The old `cleanup_proposals` migration is removed in the same bump: a
    partial unreserve wrote the shortfall into `proposal.value`, so a second run would unreserve
    the full bond again, and nothing in-repo still schedules it. If the pot cannot cover an
    approved proposal, the migration defers it, logs a warning naming the index and amount, and
    keeps the legacy storage. **Before enacting the upgrade, a chain whose pot cannot cover an
    approved proposal must pay it out manually, fund the pot, or remove the approval: the storage
    version is then 1, so a later upgrade does not retry deferred entries.** It is wired into the
    Rococo, Asset Hub Westend, Collectives Westend and kitchensink runtimes. Pass the same
    `MaxApprovals` getter the runtime used on treasury; that constant now lives on
    `pallet_bounties::Config` and only bounds `BountyApprovals` there.

    Removed the deprecated `Config::RuntimeEvent` associated type from `pallet_bounties::Config`;
    external runtimes must bound `frame_system::Config` with
    `RuntimeEvent: From<pallet_bounties::Event>`.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-bounties
  bump: major
- name: pallet-child-bounties
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-tips
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-treasury
  bump: major
